# ZHOURI_2_54_2x20_Female — component wrapper: local KiCad symbol + footprint, LCSC pinned
# in properties (feeds the JLC BOM/CPL fields). J-EXP board-to-board FEMALE socket on the
# CNC Expansion (2026-07-26 mezzanine stack — mates the Featherweight's
# BOOMELE_2_54_2x20_Male header below; supersedes the C9043 IDC ribbon pair).
#
# Part: ZHOURI (Shanghai Zhouri) "2.54-2*20", LCSC C2977589. BOOMELE's own 2x20 female
# (C50982) had a stock of 2 on 2026-07-26 — dead; this is the best-stocked 8.5mm 2x20
# socket instead (deviation from the BOOMELE-family preference, stock-forced). Stock check
# 2026-07-26: 48,410 pcs LCSC / 4,989 pcs JLC; Basic/Extended flag not shown by either
# search UI, re-verify at order time. $0.18-0.25 @ 160+.
# Drawing (LCSC datasheet 3b14debf07a36a1891d4e7bca44d0f5d.pdf "2.54-2*N", 2026-07-26) +
# 3D-model cross-check (WRL z −3.2..+8.50mm):
#   insulator height 8.5 +/- 0.2mm, solder tail 3.2 +/- 0.2mm (0.65 x 0.4mm section)
#   pitch 2.54, rows 2.54 apart, body 51.05 x 5.08mm; footprint bbox ~51.2 x 5.08mm
# MATED stack (see both BOARD-INTENT.md files): board-to-board separation 11.04mm fully
# seated (male base 2.54 + insulator 8.5), male pin engagement 6.0mm. MOUNTING ON THE
# EXPANSION: body inserted from BELOW the board (openings down toward the Featherweight),
# tails soldered on the Expansion's TOP face (3.2mm tail − 1.6mm board = 1.6mm protrusion).
# The FOOTPRINT is placed UNFLIPPED on F.Cu — do NOT flip it to the back side: the part is
# unkeyed/symmetric, so pad numbering is footprint-defined, and the unflipped footprint's
# pad n sits exactly over the male's pin n (identical pad-numbering geometry, verified).
# A flipped placement mirrors the columns (pad 1 lands over male pin 39) — the classic
# stacking bug. 3D-model caveat: rendered unflipped the body shows ABOVE the board; a
# render-side transform may flip it for presentation, but never edit the footprint pairing.
#
# Pad numbering (verified from the footprint, rot 0): pad 1 = WEST end SOUTH row; odd pins
# south row, even pins north row, columns 1/2 .. 39/40 west->east.

